{
  "tema": 7061,
  "slug": "poco-un-poco",
  "titulo": "Difference between poco and un poco",
  "subtitulo": "Como poco (not much) vs como un poco (a bit).",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Poco = little, not much (negative); un poco = a bit (positive). With nouns: poco / poca / pocos / pocas agree; un poco de + uncountable noun.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Poco** and **un poco** both talk about a small quantity, but the feeling is opposite:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Feeling",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "poco",
              "_little, not much_: negative",
              "Como poco. (I don't eat much.)"
            ],
            [
              "un poco",
              "_a bit, some_: positive",
              "Como un poco. (I eat a bit.)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In English, **poco** often sounds better as a negative: **gano poco** = _I don't earn much_. Add **muy** to stress it: **muy poco**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**With verbs**, both are adverbs and never change: **duermo poco**, **descansé un poco**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**With nouns**, **poco** is an adjective and agrees: **poco dinero**, **poca grasa**, **pocos amigos**, **pocas olas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Un poco de** + an uncountable noun = _a bit of_: **un poco de agua**, **un poco de tiempo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Un poco** + adjective often softens a criticism: **está un poco caro**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **poco** is a glass half empty; **un poco** is a glass with something in it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "A mediodía siempre como ==poco==.",
              "en": "I never eat much at noon."
            },
            {
              "es": "A mediodía como ==un poco== y sigo trabajando.",
              "en": "At noon I eat a bit and keep working."
            },
            {
              "es": "Este mes gané ==poco==.",
              "en": "I didn't earn much this month."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ahorré ==un poco== para las vacaciones.",
              "en": "I saved a bit for vacation."
            },
            {
              "es": "Dormimos ==muy poco== por el ruido.",
              "en": "We slept very little because of the noise."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy hay ==pocas== olas.",
              "en": "There aren't many waves today."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Me das ==un poco de== agua?",
              "en": "Can you give me a bit of water?"
            },
            {
              "es": "La tabla está ==un poco== cara.",
              "en": "The board is a bit expensive."
            }
          ]
